#: ../../../source/communication.rst:112
msgid "ESP-NOW Remote"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:114
msgid "The paired remote sends each ``ControlPacket`` directly over ESP-NOW to the ESP32-S3. Unlike the Mega UART link, ESP-NOW does not use the ``0xAA 0xFF`` frame header, XOR checksum or ``0x55`` footer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:120
msgid "``ControlPacket`` carries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:122
msgid "Message type: control (0x01) or heartbeat (0x02)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:123
msgid "Throttle, strafe and rotation, each from -100 to 100"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:124
msgid "Button bitmask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:125
msgid "Sequence number (the robot rejects duplicate and out-of-order values)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:126
msgid "CRC-8 over the preceding packet bytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:128
msgid "The hub listens on ESP-NOW channel 1. Set ``ESPNOW_REMOTE_MAC`` in ``components/SRV_EspNow/cfg/s3_devkit/EspNow_Cfg.h`` to the paired remote's MAC address; the checked-in address is a placeholder. The receive callback rejects packets from other MAC addresses, packets with the wrong length, invalid CRCs, and unknown message types. Accepted packets enter an eight-packet queue and ``SRV_EspNow_Update()`` hands them to the app handler, which forwards them to ``Robot`` through ``SWC_Robot_OnRemote()`` from the main loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/communication.rst:130
msgid "The ESP32-S3 accepts remote commands only while the control source is ``REMOTE``. ``Robot`` rejects duplicate and out-of-order sequence numbers. A heartbeat updates the link timer while keeping the last control command active. If no accepted remote packet arrives for 500 ms, the robot clears the command and stops the drive. The sequence check is reset after a link timeout or control-source change so a restarted remote can begin again at sequence 0."
msgstr ""
